# --- Secrets: never commit ---
.env
dns_sync/cloudflare_API.md

# --- ERP-owned data (real customer and accounting data) ---
sqlserver-backups/
pg-backups/
var/

# --- Customer material ---
# docs/ holds written documentation and nothing else. Anything else dropped
# in there -- a WhatsApp export, an EPF receipt, a scan of a payslip -- is
# real customer or employee data and must not be committed.
#
# This is deliberately a whitelist. The previous rule named one folder
# (Docs/whatsapp_chats/) and stopped matching the moment the directory was
# renamed to lowercase, which is how those files reached the repository.
docs/**
!docs/**/
!docs/**/*.md
# ...except this one, which is customer leads that happen to be markdown.
docs/whatsapp_chats/

# --- Runtime / build output ---
session_data.json
session_data.json.lock
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
npm-debug.log*
.flask.log
*.log

# --- Local scratch ---
*.bak-*
.smoke/
.ab/
